<!--
    The test run reporter's grammar, compiled and exercised without Unity
    (issue #167).

    `DxTerminalTestRunReporter.cs.txt` is C# that only ever compiled inside a
    host Unity project, so nothing in CI ran it: a rename, a moved cap or a
    syntax error reached a developer machine first (#164). This project compiles
    that exact file - linked, not copied, so it cannot drift - against a
    hand-written stand-in for the Unity types it uses, drives the real callbacks
    end to end, and writes the claims it produced. The node side
    (`grammar.test.mjs`) decodes them with the real reader, which is the only
    place the two halves of the contract meet.

    The stand-in carries only members the real API has, so the compile is a gate
    rather than a mock. It is not a substitute for the host matrix: whether a
    real editor accepts the file on a given version is what #164's
    clean-project matrix answers.

    LangVersion 9.0 is the floor: 2021.3 is the package minimum, so a dev tool
    using newer syntax in a consumer's project would break their editor.
    Run via `npm run mcp:grammar`.
-->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>9.0</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <!-- No PackageReference on purpose, so nothing here can break because a
         package moved. The restore is not free: building net8.0 under a newer
         SDK pulls the 8.0 targeting and apphost packs from nuget.org, which is
         why the CI job caches ~/.nuget/packages. -->
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
    <!-- Built against the oldest runtime this gate can be built on, run on
         whatever the machine has. A contributor with only a newer SDK installed
         must not have to install a second runtime to run the gate. -->
    <RollForward>LatestMajor</RollForward>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="../DxTerminalTestRunReporter.cs.txt" Link="DxTerminalTestRunReporter.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
